        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 231.51,
          "end": 233.49,
          "en": "Now how this is happening, first of all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 233.49,
          "end": 234.62,
          "en": "for every time we have an integer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 234.62,
          "end": 236.49,
          "en": "we have a class type, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 236.49,
          "end": 238.32,
          "en": "Now what is happening here is example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 238.32,
          "end": 241.05,
          "en": "let's say if you want to store this INT NUM variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 241.05,
          "end": 243.87,
          "en": "which is a primitive type in this, instead of saying eight,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 243.87,
          "end": 246.66,
          "en": "let me just do that here, I will parse NUM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 246.66,
          "end": 250.23,
          "en": "Now what we are doing is we are taking a primitive value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 250.23,
          "end": 251.91,
          "en": "and storing that in a object.",
